## MCP Gateway

The MCP Gateway is the main security boundary.

Required controls:

- strong authentication
- TLS / mTLS
- RBAC
- tool allowlist
- input validation
- policy checks
- rate limits
- project scoping
- repository scoping
- optional human approval
- output filtering
- secret redaction
- audit logging

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    REQ["Cloud Agent Request"]
    AUTH["Authentication"]
    RBAC["RBAC"]
    POLICY["Policy Check"]
    APPROVAL["Optional Human Approval"]
    EXEC["Local Tool Execution"]
    FILTER["Output Filtering"]
    RESP["Return Result"]

    REQ --> AUTH --> RBAC --> POLICY --> APPROVAL --> EXEC --> FILTER --> RESP
```

## Tool Design

Prefer narrow tools.

```text
GOOD
--------------------------------
run_tests(project_id)
get_git_diff(project_id)
read_repository_file(project_id, path)
get_pod_logs(namespace, pod)
query_database_readonly(query_id, params)
create_feature_branch(project_id)

BAD
--------------------------------
run_arbitrary_shell(command)
execute_raw_sql(sql)
ssh(host, command)
access_internal_network(host, port)
```

